    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="1268" n="1254" xml:id="pg1254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./10–1044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the Advisory Council for
                        Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-10T19:00:00+01:00">October 10, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—7 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>700. Italian Foreign Office, having received information of increasing German
                    persecutions in northern Italy involving barbarous tortures and massacre of
                    hostages, has asked ACC<anchor n="41" xml:id="d799-f1"/> whether fresh warning
                    could not be given Germany that such conduct will not pass unnoticed. It
                    proposes that such a warning be given by Allies and Italian Government
                    simultaneously and publicized through radio and press. ACC will be instructed to
                    inform Foreign Office that question has been referred to the two
                    Governments.</p>
                <p>Text of Italian memo of particulars sent by pouch.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d799-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
